WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.269
dot optionally rounds each FP32 input to FP16 with __float2half_rn and converts it back with __half2float. total remains FP32.

00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:19.679
This starter isolates rounding while its arrays remain FP32; the model separately compares storage formats.

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:23.235
Read FP32.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.396
Fetch a value from the input array.

00:00:25.616 --> 00:00:26.875
Optionally round.

00:00:27.095 --> 00:00:30.060
Convert to FP16 and back before adding.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.136
Accumulate FP32.

00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:34.297
Keep total in the wider format.

00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:40.072
Registers hold a thread’s working operands and accumulator.

00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:45.903
Rounding an operand can change a sum even when the accumulation stays FP32.

00:00:46.123 --> 00:00:50.603
This example uses conversions and scalar additions, not tensor cores.
